// R8 - `.read` takes no arguments, and the check has to exist because the
// argument was not merely ignored: it was DROPPED. `bump()` below was emitted
// into the C and never called, so a side effect the user wrote disappeared.
//
// `.write` and `.strobe` have checked their arity since the rune era. `.read`
// not checking is the shape that makes a partial rule worse than no rule: the
// two neighbours diagnose, so the third reads as diagnosed too.
rune status: u16 at 0xDFF002 read;

fn bump() -> int { println(99); return 1; }

fn main() { println(status.read(bump()) as int); }
